---
/* What this page rests on — and a way to actually get there.

   This is the more important half of the sources work, and it was found by
   accident while measuring the other half. Defranceski does not only have the
   best sources page in the estate; it has THIRTY-NINE PAGES THAT DECLARE
   WHICH SOURCES THEY REST ON, each naming source ids that must resolve in
   sources.json. Nothing else in the estate has anything like it.

   That is why its sources page does not drift. A sources page is otherwise
   the one page in an archive that goes stale silently, because nothing breaks
   when it does — commits to each archive's data since its sources page was
   last touched ran Lerena 302, Defranceski 121, Luwinski 93, Blazevic 64,
   Booyzen 57, D'Arcy 29. A page that names its sources by id cannot drift
   that way: the id has to exist, and a reader who follows it arrives at the
   entry rather than at the bibliography's front door.

   Defranceski's own comment records why the outward link was added, and it is
   the whole argument of this file: the block «used to link only inward, to
   this site's own bibliography, which answered "what is this" and never
   "take me to it"».

   The honest fallback matters as much as the link. Where a source is not
   online, this says where the thing physically is rather than silently
   printing nothing — because "we hold a photocopy in the source library" and
   "you can read it this minute" are different answers and a reader is owed
   the difference.

     ids       source ids, in the order this page wants them read. An id that
               does not resolve is DROPPED and counted, never rendered as a
               blank: see `missing`, which a build gate reads.
     sources   the archive's sources rows — the same array its sources page
               groups. Handed in rather than imported, because the shape and
               the location of that file differ across the estate.
     note      one line of the page's own words about its sources.
     href      where "the full bibliography" goes. Default /sources/.
     u         the archive's url helper.
*/
const {
  ids = [], sources = [], note, href = "/sources/", u = (p) => p,
  label = "What this page rests on",
} = Astro.props;

const byId = new Map(sources.map((s) => [s.id, s]));
const list = ids.map((i) => byId.get(i)).filter(Boolean);
const missing = ids.filter((i) => !byId.has(i));

const host = (url) => String(url || "").replace(/^https?:\/\/(www\.)?/, "").replace(/\/.*$/, "");
const where = (s) => [s.kind, s.where || s.holder].filter(Boolean).join(" · ");
---
{list.length > 0 && (
  <section class="srcblock" data-missing={missing.length || null}>
    <div class="lab">{label}</div>
    <div class="srclist">
      {list.map((s) => (
        <div class="srcitem">
          <a href={u(`${href}#${s.id}`)}>{s.title}</a>
          {where(s) && <span>{where(s)}</span>}
          {s.url
            ? <a class="srcout" href={s.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{host(s.url)} &#8599;</a>
            : <span class="srcheld">{s.held
                ? s.held
                : "not online — see the bibliography for where it is held"}</span>}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    {note && <p class="cap" style="margin-top:14px">{note}</p>}
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:10px"><a href={u(href)}>The full bibliography, with what
    each source gave and where it is weak →</a></p>
  </section>
)}

<style is:global>
  .srcblock .srcout {
    display: block; margin-top: 3px;
    font: 400 11px/1.3 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .02em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .srcblock .srcheld {
    display: block; margin-top: 3px;
    font: 400 11px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-3); letter-spacing: .02em;
  }
</style>
